<section class="phero"><div class="phero-bg"><img src="/assets/img/photos/storm-surf.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/storm-surf-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/storm-surf.webp 1200w" sizes="100vw" width="1200" height="800" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" data-parallax="0.1"></div><div class="wrap phero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><i aria-hidden="true">›</i><a href="/island-claim-tools/">Claim tools</a><i aria-hidden="true">›</i><span aria-current="page">Hurricane Deductible Calculator</span></nav><p class="tag">Free calculator</p><h1>Hurricane Deductible Calculator for Island Homeowners</h1><p class="lede">A 2% hurricane deductible sounds small until it’s multiplied by island rebuilding values. See your deductible in real dollars and what a storm claim would pay.</p></div></section>
<section class="sec tool-sec"><div class="wrap">
<div class="tool" data-tool="deduct">
  <div class="tool-head"><span>Hurricane deductible calculator</span><i>Percentage vs. flat</i></div>
  <div class="tool-body">
    <div class="tool-in">
      <div><label for="w-a">Dwelling coverage (Coverage A)</label><input id="w-a" name="cova" inputmode="decimal" value="720000"><span class="hint">From your declarations page.</span></div>
      <div class="row2">
        <div><label for="w-p">Hurricane deductible</label><select id="w-p" name="pct"><option value="1">1%</option><option value="2" selected>2%</option><option value="3">3%</option><option value="5">5%</option><option value="10">10%</option></select></div>
        <div><label for="w-f">All-other-perils deductible ($)</label><input id="w-f" name="flat" inputmode="decimal" value="2500"></div>
      </div>
      <div><label for="w-l">Estimated hurricane damage</label><input id="w-l" name="loss" inputmode="decimal" value="38500"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="tool-out" aria-live="polite">
      <div class="out-big"><small>Your hurricane deductible in dollars</small><b data-o="pd">$0</b></div>
      <div class="stack" aria-hidden="true"><span class="s3"></span><span class="s1"></span></div>
      <div class="legend"><span><i class="s3"></i>You pay</span><span><i class="s1"></i>Policy pays</span></div>
      <div class="out-rows">
        <div><span>Payment with the % deductible</span><b data-o="pdpay">$0</b></div>
        <div><span>Payment if the flat deductible applied</span><b data-o="flatpay">$0</b></div>
        <div><span>Extra out-of-pocket from the % deductible</span><b data-o="diff">$0</b></div>
      </div>
      <p class="out-msg" data-o="below"></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
<p class="hint">For planning only. Results depend on the figures you enter and your policy’s terms; they are not a quote, an appraisal or legal advice. Default figures are illustrative.</p></div></section>
<div class="wrap layout"><article class="prose">
<h2>Why percentage deductibles catch people off guard</h2>
<p>Many island homeowners carry a separate hurricane deductible written as a percentage of dwelling coverage. Because rebuilding costs here are high, Coverage A limits are high too — and so is the deductible. In the illustrative default above, 2% of $720,000 is $14,400, not the $2,500 that applies to most other losses.</p>
<h2>When it applies</h2>
<p>Policies define the trigger differently. Some apply the hurricane deductible only when the National Weather Service has issued a hurricane watch or warning for the islands, others to any named storm, and some for a set period afterward. Wind damage from a Kona low or trade-wind gusts usually falls under the regular deductible. Read the endorsement and our guide to <a href="/hawaii-claim-guides/hurricane-deductibles-in-hawaii/">hurricane deductibles in Hawaii</a>.</p>
<h2>How it affects an appraisal decision</h2>
<p>The deductible doesn’t change the amount of loss a panel decides, but it changes what you receive. A loss just above a large deductible may not be worth disputing; one well above it often is. Combine this result with the <a href="/island-claim-tools/claim-gap-fee-estimator/">claim gap &amp; fee estimator</a>.</p>
<h2>Questions about this tool</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Does the percentage apply to contents too?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="a"><p>The dollar amount is usually calculated from Coverage A but applied to the whole hurricane loss. Check your policy’s endorsement for the exact wording.</p></div></details><details><summary>Can I lower my hurricane deductible?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="a"><p>Options depend on the carrier and are usually available at renewal. A lower deductible typically means a higher premium.</p></div></details></div><h2>More free tools</h2><div class="related"><a href="/island-claim-tools/claim-timeline-builder/"><small>Planner</small><span>Claim Timeline Builder</span><svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a><a href="/island-claim-tools/appraisal-readiness-check/"><small>Checklist</small><span>Appraisal Readiness Check</span><svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a><a href="/island-claim-tools/condo-deductible-share-calculator/"><small>Calculator</small><span>Condo Deductible Share Calculator</span><svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M